You are right. It was only built on that patch; the two touched the
same lines of mail-tag.sh, and nothing more. The superseded tag needs
nothing from the Committed header. I will not pursue "[PATCH]
notmuch: Tag patches reported committed" [1] further.

> Let's keep this really simple. Let's get automatic supersession tracking
> working, and go from there.

Done, as "[PATCH v3] notmuch: Tag series a later version replaces"
[2]. It is a single patch that applies to b/dev@upstream on its own.
It tags the whole thread that a revised series names on its "Link to
vN: id:<message-id>" line, and hides nothing; "not tag:superseded"
filters the old threads out.

v3 drops the manual Superseded-by trailer patch that "[PATCH v2 0/2]
notmuch: Tag superseded series" [3] still carried, so the hook needs
no git and takes no input beyond what a revised series already
writes. The seven threads that no Link line names stay untagged for
now. We can return to them once this works for you.

I ran the hook from this commit against a copy of my notmuch database.
It tags 27 threads, 136 messages, each an older version of a series,
and a second run tags the same set. After you apply it, one "notmuch
new" tags them, since post-new already runs mail-tag.sh.

